#ETH  A single return of 320,000!! Good news, Xiao Deng, who was losing, has made money. The Ethereum spike arranged a perfect entry at 3020 for the buy order. Xiao Deng is very execution-oriented. When he found me at noon, he was able to perfectly match my rhythm. I told Xiao Deng that this position is a strong support, very easy to set a stop loss, with a small loss at 3010, heavily investing and rolling over, a single order of 320,000 gained.

#zec  90% of people in the cryptocurrency world do not understand: those who truly make money abide by these 6 iron rules. The cryptocurrency world is like a river and lake; some become rich overnight while others lose everything.
I once lost everything and fell into despair until I reunited with an old friend who immigrated to Canada, which changed my fate in the cryptocurrency world!

#beat  He started with hundreds of thousands and in just a few years made several tens of millions, while I was struggling to breathe due to losses at that time.
At the dinner, his words struck me like a hammer: "Most people in the cryptocurrency world are puppets controlled by emotions. Stay calm; this is a cash machine."

I reviewed his experiences and summarized 6 iron rules, which helped me stand firm:
1. Fast rise, slow fall = large funds accumulating, don't be scared away by a temporary drop, just keep the rhythm;
2. Fast fall, slow rise = the market makers are offloading; a sharp drop followed by weak rebounds, don’t be greedy and act as a buyer;
3. Volume at the top or continuation of the upward trend, if there's no volume at the top, quickly withdraw; volume is the market's weather vane;
4. A single large volume at the bottom is often a bait; continuous volume is a safe signal, consensus needs to be gradually formed;
5. Trading cryptocurrencies is trading emotions; consensus determines price, and volume is the most real reflection of consensus; don’t be misled by candlestick charts;
6. "Nothing" is the key to victory: no obsession, no greed, no fear; those who wait for opportunities with empty positions deserve to take on big trends.
The true enemy in trading is never external news, data, or major actions but the fluctuations of the heart.

Opportunities and risks coexist in the cryptocurrency world; only by understanding risks, staying calm, and adhering to conservative strategies can one carve out a place in this river and lake.
Those who can survive and still earn in the market have always been the ones who dare to reach out first.
